/-! # Lifting sections of high powers of a fibre-ample line bundle

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, Tag 0D2M, lemma-ample-on-fibre,
the final assertion with the coherent module equal to the structure sheaf.
(blueprint: lem-trf-ample-fibre-section-lifting).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- Sections of all sufficiently high powers on the fibre lift over open neighbourhoods
of the base point. The pullback of a section is the actual tensor section `1 ⊗ t`,
restricted to the whole fibre and followed by the fixed recursive tensor-power comparison.
The fibre's invertibility witness comes from `invertible_pullback_tensor`, so it adds
no hypothesis. Natural exponents encode exactly the integers above a nonnegative bound.

Source: Stacks Project, Cohomology of Schemes, Tag 0D2M, lemma-ample-on-fibre,
final assertion with F = O_Z; Tag 02OD for the local dictionary.
(blueprint: lem-trf-ample-fibre-section-lifting).

Proof, following the node's eight steps:
1. Work over A = O_{S,s}. Choose a Noetherian affine chart at s by pqf-def-locnoeth;
lem-weil-pbc-spec-local-ring-canonical-morphism identifies A with its localization.
Contracting an ideal to the chart and localizing its finite generators proves A Noetherian
(def-weil-pbc-noetherian-ring). Choose generators a_1,...,a_r of its maximal ideal m;
r = 0 is allowed.
2. Set X = Z times_S Spec A, N = h^*L and E_d = N^{tensor d}. Properness survives base change
(lem-weil-pbc-proper-fp-permanence). Affine quasi-compactness and finite-type preservation
of Noetherianity make Z, X and the closed fibre Noetherian
(lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs, lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian).
Invertible pullback and tensor products identify i^*E_d with L_s^{tensor d}, and E_d is
coherent by pqf-lem-coherent-ft-locnoeth and lem-weil-pbc-invertible-pullback-tensor.
3. Put J = m O_X. Its powers are generated by finite families of monomials in the a_j.
Coherent kernels and cokernels give coherent quotients J^n/J^{n+1}
(lem-weil-pbc-coherent-kernel-cokernel-locnoeth). Closed-immersion coherent equivalence
regards them as coherent G_n on the closed fibre
(lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-coherent-equivalence). Their graded sum G is generated
by 1 in degree zero over k[T_1,...,T_r], with T_j acting by a_j modulo the next power.
Changing representatives changes products by the next ideal power, so this is well defined.
4. Graded Serre vanishing (lem-weil-pbc-formal-systems-graded-vanishing) gives a single d0
with H^1(G tensor L_s^{tensor d}) = 0 for d >= d0. Each G_n is a retract of G, so its
corresponding H^1 vanishes for all n with the same bound, without commuting cohomology
with an infinite direct sum (pqf-def-cohomology).
5. For Q_n = E_d/J^n E_d the successive quotient sequence has kernel
(J^n/J^{n+1}) tensor E_d. This is checked where E_d is trivial and glues. The closed-immersion
projection and cohomology formulas (lem-pc-closed-immersion-coherent-cohomology) identify
its H^1 with the group vanishing in step 4. The long exact sequence (pqf-def-cohomology)
makes H^0(Q_{n+1}) -> H^0(Q_n) surjective, hence H^0(Q_k) -> H^0(Q_1) surjective for k >= 1.
6. Apply lem-weil-pbc-ml-cohomology-powers-ideal in degree zero to E_d and m. For large k
the image of H^0(Q_k) -> H^0(Q_1) equals that of H^0(E_d) -> H^0(Q_1). Step 5 therefore
makes the latter map surjective. The stabilization index may depend on d, but d0 does not.
7. The uncompleted comparison of lem-weil-pbc-formal-functions-local-dictionary identifies
this map with the canonical direct-image stalk to fibre-sections map. The defining
restriction formula of def-weil-pbc-formal-fibre-cohomology sends a neighbourhood germ
to the pulled-back section. In degree zero, kernels in an injective resolution identify
cohomology and its maps with ordinary sections (pqf-def-cohomology).
8. Choose a preimage of the prescribed t in the direct-image stalk and represent its germ
on an open neighbourhood U of s (def-weil-pbc-module-stalk). This is a section on f^{-1}U,
and its pullback is t by step 7 and def-pc-module-pullback. The fixed comparison in the
conclusion iterates the tensor comparison of lem-weil-pbc-invertible-pullback-tensor,
including its unit case. If the fibre is empty, its sole section lifts as zero.
-/
theorem exists_lift_section_of_fiber_isAmple {Z S : Scheme.{u}} (f : Z ⟶ S)
    [IsProper f] [IsLocallyNoetherian S] [CompactSpace S]
    (L : Z.Modules) [L.IsInvertible] (s : S)
    (hL : @IsAmple (f.fiber s) ((tensorPullback (f.fiberι s)).obj L)
      ((invertible_pullback_tensor (f.fiberι s)).1 L).2) :
    ∃ d₀ : ℕ, ∀ d : ℕ, d₀ ≤ d →
      ∀ t : Γ(((tensorPullback (f.fiberι s)).obj L).tensorPow d, ⊤),
        ∃ (U : S.Opens) (hs : s ∈ U) (t' : Γ(L.tensorPow d, f ⁻¹ᵁ U)),
          (boundaryPullbackPowIso (f.fiberι s) L d).hom.app ⊤
            (((tensorPullback (f.fiberι s)).obj (L.tensorPow d)).val.map
              (homOfLE (fun x _ ↦ Eq.mpr
                (congrArg (fun y : S ↦ y ∈ U) (f.fiberHomeo s x).property) hs)).op
              (tensorPullbackSection (f.fiberι s) (L.tensorPow d) (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) t')) = t := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
